From f2b0acbc307a8ab780e9ca1c0a44f6015ad79469 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nyyks <janik.wyder@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:25:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat: CloudDeck-Client encrypted microphone stream (protocol
 v1)

Client -> host Opus audio on the existing audio UDP port, AES-128-GCM with
the session key (nonce domain 'CM'), negotiated via SDP x-ss-mic.version,
RTSP SETUP streamid=mic and ANNOUNCE x-ss-mic.enabled. Decoded audio is
played into a virtual source 'CloudDeck Microphone' (null sink + remap
source via pactl). Stock clients are unaffected. Disable with CLOUDDECK_MIC=0.

Spec: CloudDeck-Client docs/protocol-extensions.md section 1.
